  abstract={This article presents a 2-read/write (2RW) pseudo dual-port (PDP) static random access memory (SRAM) macro implemented in advanced 3 nm Fin-FET technology, achieving a competitive bit density of 19.87 Mbit/mm2 for advanced nodes. To address challenges in process scaling, reliability under process voltage temperature variations, and dynamic power consumption, two design techniques are introduced: 1) metal wire resistance tracking for adaptive between margin optimization, and 2) sequential access-aware dynamic power reduction to achieve power savings under specific conditions. Post-layout simulations and silicon measurements validate the proposed techniques, demonstrating stable operation across a wide voltage–frequency range and reducing macro-level dynamic power by up to 12%. These innovations significantly enhance performance, power, and area for high-density, low-power applications.},
